# Givers who lie (docs/DESIGN.md, "Story blocks"; Missions/Story/RZ_Grey.c): when you found what a
# brief left out, any leader of the giver's faction can hear it. Taking it public costs that faction
# 1 morale (capped) and an outpost giver 5 loyalty. It pays nothing: the truth is the payoff.
# The leader says what telling costs before you choose (docs/WRITING.md, "Grey choices").

conv haven.leader.brief_lie
for leader:haven
when knows:brieflie.haven
topic "The job I took left something out."
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say Go on, then. If one of ours told you half of it, the house should hear the other half. That's how a house stays a house.
  say It'll cost them, whoever it was. People stop trusting the voice that hands out the work. Say it or don't. It's your call, not mine.
  > @tell Here's what I found. -> told
  > @keep I'll keep it to myself. -> kept

node told
  say Right. I'll read it out at supper, after the name. Nobody will enjoy it, and somebody will go quiet for a week.
  do call:brief_public
  > @back It's better they know. -> hub

node kept
  say Your call. Some things go quieter if you let them, and some go bad. We'll see which this is.
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv bastion.leader.brief_lie
for leader:bastion
when knows:brieflie.bastion
topic "That briefing wasn't straight."
prio reaction
voice bastion

node start
  say A briefing that wasn't straight. If it came off one of our posts, it goes in a report, and the report goes up to the stronghold.
  say It'll cost somebody: that post's word is worth less after. Keep it short and keep it accurate.
  > @tell Here's what it left out. -> told
  > @keep Leave it out of the record. -> kept

node told
  say Received. It goes up the chain, such as the chain is. The commander concerned will be asked about it at the roll.
  do call:brief_public
  > @back Good. Let me ask something else. -> hub

node kept
  say Not reported, then. I didn't hear it either. That's how it goes in the log: it doesn't.
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv redhand.leader.brief_lie
for leader:redhand
when knows:brieflie.redhand
topic "Somebody sold me a job short."
prio reaction
voice redhand

node start
  say Somebody sold you a job short? Careful. The crew loves a story like that, and it'll want a name to go with it.
  say Tell it, and it's round the fires by dark and somebody's page gets longer. Keep it, and you're holding something on them. Both are worth something.
  > @tell Tell the crew. I want it heard. -> told
  > @keep Let it lie. I'll hold on to it. -> kept

node told
  say That'll go round the fires by dark. Somebody's evening just got a lot worse.
  do call:brief_public
  > @back Good. Something else. -> hub

node kept
  say Good. A secret's worth more kept. Remember who owes you for it, because they'll try to forget.
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv halcyon.leader.brief_lie
for leader:halcyon
when knows:brieflie.halcyon
topic "That brief left something out."
prio reaction
voice halcyon

node start
  say A discrepancy in a brief. The lab takes discrepancies seriously, on paper.
  say On the record, the director is told and whoever wrote the brief answers for it. Off the record, it joins a great many other things.
  > @tell Put it on the record. -> told
  > @keep Leave it off the record. -> kept

node told
  say Recorded, with the date. The director will be told. The director won't thank either of us.
  do call:brief_public
  > @back That's fine by me. -> hub

node kept
  say Off the record, then. There's a great deal off the record. It's the largest file we keep.
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub
